timestamp=2026-11-04T15:20:37.862Z level=INFO run=7dbbc1d1 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# That still doesn't give 1221.0. But maybe salary_amount in the file is irrelevant? Or maybe it's the total?\n# Another row: row 2, employee 84731091580 (bad) - but let's look at a good one. Row 3: emp 88032898468, rate 27, hrs 4, bonus 760, sal 621. 4*27+760=868+760? 108+760=868. sal is 621, not matching.\n# Row 6: 97042365105, rate 27, hrs 2, bonus 790, sal 1053. 54+790=844. sal=1053.\n# Something's off. Let us look at more examples.\nimport pandas as pd\nemployees = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/employees.csv')\ntimesheet = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/timesheet.csv')\n\nfor i in range(5):\n    row = timesheet.iloc[i]\n    emp_id = row['employee_id']\n    if emp_id not in employees['PESEL'].values:\n        print(f'[{i}] SKIP bad emp {emp_id}')\n        continue\n    emp = employees[employees['PESEL'] == emp_id].iloc[0]\n    calc_total = row['hours_worked'] * emp['hourly_rate'] + row['bonus']\n    print(f'[{i}] emp={emp_id} hrs={row[\"hours_worked\"]} rate={emp[\"hourly_rate\"]} bonus={row[\"bonus\"]} sal_amt={row[\"salary_amount\"]} calc_total={calc_total}')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
