timestamp=2026-11-04T15:25:35.742Z level=INFO run=7dbbc1d1 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# The salary_amount in timesheet does not match the formula. Maybe salary_amount is the total salary to be paid?\n# But the numbers don't add up. Or maybe hours_worked are scaled? Or maybe the bonus is already included? Or maybe salary_amount is (hours * something else). Let us look at actual examples differently.\n# Or maybe the timesheet's \"salary_amount\" is what we need to compute as total? Wait - let us read the task again.\n# \"calculate the total monthly salary for each employee for every month. The total salary is the sum of:\n# (total hours worked in the month × hourly rate) + any bonuses earned for completed tasks in that month.\"\n# So we must compute this. But the dataset has timesheet with hours_worked, performed_tasks, employee_id, maybe salary already computed? Also has \"salary_amount\" and \"bonus\" columns. That is confusing. Also the task says \"final salary values should be rounded to the nearest integer using standard mathematical rounding.\"\n# And validation compares our answer against ground truth (gt). But we don't have gt. So we must infer from the full dataset and task description correctly.\n# Maybe the \"salary_amount\" in timesheet is the base salary (hours * rate) and \"bonus\" is bonus. And the total is salary_amount + bonus? Let us check.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
