timestamp=2026-11-04T15:52:34.925Z level=INFO run=7dbbc1d1 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# That matches the first value for 68011810139. So grouping by calendar month (year,month) gives correct sums. The billing period constraint in the task - does this affect our grouping? The task states \"For each month, the billing period for all employees starts on the same day of the week inherited from the dataset's earliest record.\" If the billing period starts mid-month (e.g. Tuesday), records before that Tuesday might belong to previous billing period. But in our data, earliest is 2025-03-04 (Tue). Also all records start from 2025-03-04 onwards - so nothing is before that start. That means billing period boundaries align with how the data is partitioned here. Grouping by calendar month with standard month boundaries gives the same effective grouping given the constraints. That matches.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
